        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: шапка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "шапка (shápka) — \"a hat\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "шапка (shápka) — recorded from 1327. It is usually taken through Middle High German schapël from Old French chape, chapel, from Latin cappa, \"a hooded cloak\"; Vasmer notes that West Slavic has only č-, as in Polish czapka, which troubles that account."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
